let's take a quick look at how to deploy  Python 3 applications to Google App  Engine I have a Python 3 application  that runs great on my local machine and  I want to deploy to App Engine all my  dependencies are listed in my  requirements text file to deploy our  code go to cloud.google.com sign in to  your google account if you haven't done  so already and then go to my console  make sure you sign up for the free trial  if you haven't done that yet now go to  select a project and create a project  give your project a name and click  create then go to the compute engine  section and make sure billing is enabled  if you don't have the Google Cloud SDK  installed on your computer  see the link in the description for how  to install it create a file called a PMO  with the following information we are  using Python 3 and unicorn to run our  server run g-cloud init to login to your  Google account now run g-cloud app  deploy to deploy your application in a  few minutes your application should be  deployed go to the URL and you can see  your application running on the cloud
 

